chapter.v:
So I 


will send, 


a fire upon Moab, and it shall devour the strongholds of Kerioth, and Moab shall die amid uproar, amid shouting and the sound of the trumpet;

those who 


trample the, 


head of the poor into the dust of the earth and turn aside the way of the afflicted; a man and his father go in to the same girl, so that my holy name is profaned;

Flight shall 


perish from, 


the swift, and the strong shall not retain his strength, nor shall the mighty save his life;

he who 


handles the, 


bow shall not stand, and he who is swift of foot shall not save himself, nor shall he who rides the horse save his life;
